"Every possible candidate" is not a finite set. Curve families are infinite (every choice of u, v, h in a PH curve is a curve; every α, c, C, κ in the aesthetic families is a curve; every bicubic can be interpolated). On top of that, G2 is a property of a join, not a species of curve: almost any family can be pushed through a G2 interpolator (PH quintics, spiro, clothoid chains, beta-splines, a fitted cubic). So "all curves that can be G2" cannot be enumerated at all — only all curves in a declared universe can.
What the repo actually guarantees (and it is strong, just narrower):
- every drawn curve comes from a table, never from recall;
- tests/test_curve_census.py forces every table entry to be either in NAMED or declared outside it with a reason;
- the showcase is exhaustive relative to its tables — every stem card, every named curve, every LAC cut at 90°/130°, every heart, every recovered spine;
